#import "../template.typ": *

= Notations <cha:Notations>

Unless otherwise specified,
we use the following notation throughout these notes.

- Lower case bold is used to denote vectors, e.g.~$vect(x) in complex^n$,
  and upper case sans serif is used to denote matrices, e.g.~$mat(A) in complex^(m times n)$.
  The entries of a vector $vect(x) in complex^n$ are denoted by~$(x_i)$,
  and those of a matrix $mat(A) in complex^(m times n)$ are denoted by~$(a_(i j))$ or~$(a_(i,j))$.

- The notations $ip(placeholder, placeholder)$ and $norm(placeholder)$ without a subscript always refer to the Euclidean inner product~@eq:induced_norm and induced norm.

- The sequence $x_1, x_2, dots$ is denoted by $(x_n)_(n in nat)$,
  or sometimes just $(x_n)$.

- The notation
  $B_R (vect(y))$
  refers to the open ball of radius $R$ centered at $vect(y)$.
